  "observations": [
    "All ten complete printed rows agree with secondary export tokens; metadata transcribed independently from page images.",
    "1091,1131,1143,1157 exhibit the same complete four-sign frame M267 M099 X M162, with X M102,M106,M104,M107 respectively.",
    "M102 has three short vertical strokes; M104 four; M106 five in one row; M107 five arranged three above two. These are graphic descriptions, not assigned numerical values or readings.",
    "2254 continues after M106 M287 M342 with M001, so M342 is not final there.",
    "4239 begins with long three-stroke M089, distinct from shorter M102, then M106 M287 M342.",
    "No row here authenticates an exact M102/M106 substitution within a complete inscription ending M287 M342. The primary evidence for substitution comes from a different frame.",
    "2659 is the potential three-sign counterpart *M102 M287 M342, but primary printing marks M102 doubtful. Doubt is not an export-only error; preserve exclusion."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No arbitrary phonetic, semantic, commodity, unit or arithmetic values assigned.",
    "The four substitutions are selected examples from an exploratory corpus analysis, not a held-out test.",
    "Printed normalized glyphs do not establish allographic relationships on original artifacts.",
    "Other references sharing the frame and the other two candidate frames were not visually authenticated in this review."
  ],
